-   When a business buys something, it can claim back the GST it paid as ITC, but only if conditions are met.

-   Section 16(2) of the CGST Act sets mostly deterministic conditions: the business has the invoice, has received the goods or services, the invoice appears in GSTR-2B, and the supplier has been paid within 180 days. That part is pure code.

-   Section 17(5) lists blocked credits: food and beverages, motor vehicles (with exceptions), club memberships, health and fitness, employee travel on vacation, construction of immovable property, personal consumption, gifts and free samples. Deciding whether an invoice line falls into one of these needs judgement over messy text. Examples:

