-   Cost of errors: a wrongly claimed ITC has to be reversed with 18% interest, plus possible penalties. Doing it too cautiously means the business overpays tax.

-   Frequency: monthly, every GSTR-3B filing, across hundreds of invoices.

-   Why now: ITC is now tied strictly to GSTR-2B, and GSTN recently rolled out the Invoice Management System (IMS). Check the exact dates before you write this.

-   Out of scope: apportioning common credits (Rules 42/43), income tax, and anything else that needs a CA's full judgement.

